    "summary": "High‑energy second set marathon with stellar Truckin' > Weather Report Prelude > Wharf Rat",
    "blurb": "The March ’73 Baltimore show delivers a monster second‑set jam chain from Truckin’ into the Weather Report Prelude and Wharf Rat, climaxing with an emotional Eyes → Morning Dew close. Jerry’s clean‑tone guitar and Keith’s sparkling keys drive the improvisations, while Phil provides a thunderous bass foundation throughout.",
    "review": "The March 26, 1973 show at the Baltimore Civic Center captures the band in top form, especially during the second set where they launch into an expansive Truckin' → Weather Report Suite Prelude jam that seamlessly morphs into Wharf Rat. Jerry’s guitar is immaculate and “cooking” throughout, delivering soaring leads and a superb solo bridge that keeps the momentum alive. Keith’s keyboards add bright, two‑cent fills that color the jams without ever overpowering the mix, while Phil’s bass locks in with a powerful groove, punctuated by emphatic ending notes that lift the band higher. Bill Kreutzmann’s drumming chugs along nicely, providing a solid rhythmic backbone for the marathon of improvisations that culminate in an emotionally charged Eyes → Morning Dew sequence to close the night. Highlights from the first set include a tight Playing In The Band and a standout Candyman solo that showcases Garcia’s phenomenal tone. Overall, this is a high‑energy, tightly executed performance with crystal‑clear soundboard fidelity, making it one of the most compelling shows of early ’73.",
